    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d653">

                <pb facs="0830" n="718" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg718"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/1959</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Fletcher</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 993</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 6, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Embassy’s telegram No.
                    1022 of May 2, 1 p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d653-f1"/> reporting that, with
                    reference to Articles 3 and 5 of the petroleum law accompanying my despatch No.
                    815 of March 1, the Department of Hacienda had issued a circular prescribing
                    that the royalty tax for March and April this year shall be paid in cash, I have
                    the honor to enclose herewith the text and translation of the circular in
                    reference.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry P. Fletcher</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d653-a1.xml" xpointer="d653-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
